3. Severe allergic reaction to other monoclonal antibodies;
4. There are cardiac clinical symptoms or diseases that are not well controlled, such as: (1) heart failure above NYHA grade 2 (2) unstable angina pectoris (3) myocardial infarction within one year (4) clinically significant supraventricular or ventricular arrhythmias requiring treatment or intervention (5) qtc\>450ms (male); Qtc\>470ms (female);
5. Patients at risk of massive bleeding
6. Abnormal coagulation function (inr\>1.5 or pt\>16s), bleeding tendency or undergoing thrombolytic or anticoagulant therapy;
7. Genetic or known to exist Acquired hemorrhage and thrombotic tendency (such as hemophilia, coagulation dysfunction, thrombocytopenia, hypersplenism, etc.) or arteriovenous thrombosis events in recent 6 months (until the first use of shr-1210);
